      "solution": "$f(t) = \\frac{100}{1 + 7e^{-\\frac{t}{4}}} = 100\\left(1 + 7e^{-\\frac{t}{4}}\\right)^{-1}$\n$\\therefore f'(t) = -100\\left(1 + 7e^{-\\frac{t}{4}}\\right)^{-2} \\times \\left(-\\frac{7}{4}e^{-\\frac{t}{4}}\\right) \\quad \\{\\text{chain rule}\\}\n= \\frac{175e^{-\\frac{t}{4}}}{\\left(1 + 7e^{-\\frac{t}{4}}\\right)^2}$",
      "ai_explanation": {
        "concept_rule": "Chain rule with negative powers: $\\frac{d}{dt}[u^{-1}] = -u^{-2} u'$.",
        "step_by_step": [
          "Rewrite $f(t) = 100(1 + 7e^{-t/4})^{-1}$.",
          "Outer derivative: $-100(1 + 7e^{-t/4})^{-2}$.",
          "Inner derivative: $\\frac{d}{dt}[1 + 7e^{-t/4}] = 7\\left(-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)e^{-t/4} = -\\frac{7}{4}e^{-t/4}$.",
          "Multiply: $-100 \\times \\left(-\\frac{7}{4}\\right) = +175$, giving $\\frac{175e^{-t/4}}{(1 + 7e^{-t/4})^2}$."
